            "children": [
              {
                "id": "ypsg0kx08wmi6mn",
                "text": "Buffers: Summary"
              }
            ],
            "id": "axlz0r5921d61pp",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "A solution containing a mixture of a weak acid and its conjugate base, or a weak base and its conjugate acid, is called a buffer solution. The presence of a weak conjugate acid-base pair provides reactants that can neutralize small amounts of strong acid or base, yielding weaker conjugate partners. The pH of a buffer solution therefore does not change significantly when a small amount of acid or base is added."
              }
            ],
            "id": "87z5cwbtu780vac",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "gpic2d9ekipi67b",
                "text": "End of Lesson Self-Assessment"
              }
            ],
            "id": "c19mj4vfjr0z4uh",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Before you take the Learning Checkpoint, please evaluate your understanding of the learning objectives for the "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "Buffers"
              },
              {
                "text": " module and use the My Response link below to ask any questions you might have about the material you would like the instructor to address. Your questions can be for clarification of the material, or further insight. Your self-evaluation and questions may also shape the discussions in class."
              }
            ],
            "id": "tefn29hj4t3cebr",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Your responses will not be graded, but will be available for your instructor."
              }
            ],
